course: dictionary
lesson: 760
title: Beach: a word with two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A beach is the area of sand or small stones next to the sea or a lake. Read the clues around it: «A seal pup alone on a beach is usually not lost» tells you a beach is a place where animals can rest, and the sea is nearby.
explain: Beach can also be a verb, a doing word. It means to bring a boat onto the sand, or for a whale to get stuck on land. «A beached whale» is a whale that has washed up on the shore and cannot get back into the sea.
explain: Think about the clues. «If the sea suddenly pulls far back from the beach, a tsunami may be coming: go to high ground at once.» The sea pulling back is a warning sign, so the words around beach tell you to act quickly and stay safe.
fact: A beach is the sand or small stones next to the sea or a lake.
fact: Waves break up rocks and shells over time, and this is how many beaches are made into sand.
fact: Tides go in and out, so the size of a beach can change during the day.
fact: Beach can also be a verb: to beach a boat means to pull it up onto the sand.
fact: Safety at the beach: swim between the red and yellow flags, or near the lifeguard, and look out for rip currents.
exercise: «The children ran down to the beach with their buckets.» What is a beach? | *The sand or small stones next to the sea | A small boat used for fishing | A rock on a mountain | A deep hole dug in a field
exercise: Freddie's cousin is at the beach in his togs. What are togs? | A sandcastle tool | *A swimming costume | A kind of beach boat | A warm winter coat
exercise: «If the sea suddenly pulls far back from the beach, a tsunami may be coming.» What should you do? | Wait for the sea to come back | Run down to the sand to look | Dig a hole in the sand | *Go to high ground at once
test: «The fishermen beached their boat on the sand before the storm.» What does beached mean here? | *Pulled the boat onto the land | Sank the boat in deep water | Tied the boat to a rock far out at sea | Painted the boat bright blue
test: «Swim between the red and yellow flags, near the lifeguard.» Why is this the best advice? | It means the lifeguard is having lunch | It shows where the biggest waves are for surfing | It shows where the sand is deepest | *It is the safest place to swim
exam: «A boy on a beach in Florida counts 12 seconds from flash to bang, so his family leaves the beach.» Why do they leave? | The beach is closing for cleaning | *The lightning is close enough to strike | The sea is too warm to swim in | They are hungry and want lunch
